-- title:
--   Two branches at supersingular points of the X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ an integer with $p \nmid M$ and $p \nmid M$ (i.e. $\neg\, p \mid M$). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, namely the $L$-subfield generated by the image of the function field $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp) = \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,(\Gamma_1(Mp))$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$, and let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ under the same coefficientwise map, assumed non-zero. Write $X = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two morphisms from the middle chart to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the subalgebras $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ (elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ (elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$). Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along the structural morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$; assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ and that the quotient $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Assume further that $z$ is the image under the canonical morphism `ιFin` of a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin})$, and that $y$ is supersingular in the following sense: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : \mathrm{chartAlgFin} \to \Omega$ with kernel the prime corresponding to $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-trivial point killed by $p$. Then the set of minimal primes of the ideal $(\varpi_z) \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is not a subsingleton; equivalently, it contains at least two distinct elements.
--
--   At a supersingular point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the valuation ring above $p$ in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, at which that fibre fails to be regular, at least two algebraic branches of the special fibre pass through the point. It is one half of the decomposition of the two-branches statement for the local structure of this model at singular points of its special fibre, and is used in the passage from failure of regularity of the fibre to the presence of two minimal primes.
